<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ros River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ros is a river of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, a right-bank tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> about 350 kilometres long, flowing past Bila Tserkva. In the 11th and 12th centuries it formed the southern defensive line of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>, where the princes built forts and settled Turkic allies such as the Torks and Berendei, known collectively as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chorni-klobuky">Chorni Klobuky</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ros-river.jpg" alt="Ros River" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yuriy Mitin at Russian Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ros_river_Sukholesi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
